    "rationale": "I diluted the late aliquots and scaled the readings back up by the dilution factor. 18 h at 10x: 0.0575, which scales to 0.575. 18 h at 4x: 0.137, which scales to 0.548. 12 h at 10x: 0.0575, which scales to 0.575. The undiluted readings were about 0.53. So the diluted results are only 3–8% higher, which is close to the noise between replicates (±0.004 at 10x, or ±0.04 once scaled up). That doesn't fit a saturated reader hiding a much denser culture. A flat plateau at about 0.53–0.55 looks like a real stationary phase. A slight non-linearity in the reader can't be ruled out, but it would be small."
